- **“comprehensive Multidisciplinary declaration of need assessment completed by the case manager identifying equipment, technology, supply, adaptation, or modification needs”**
- **“copy of the physician's order, when determined to be app…”**  

That last line was truncated in the retrieved text, so I could not confirm the full physician-order requirement from the section I pulled.

## Multidisciplinary Team documentation
From the text I retrieved, I could confirm only that the policy requires a **“comprehensive Multidisciplinary declaration of need assessment”** completed by the **case manager**. The retrieved CAP/DA section did **not** spell out every team member’s documentation duties in full.

For context, the CAP comprehensive multidisciplinary assessment section **3K-2:5.4** lists assessment domains that feed into the plan, including:
- contact information;
- diagnosis and history;
- medications and precautions;
- skin;
- neurological;
- sensory and communication;
- pain;
- musculoskeletal;
- cardio-respiratory;
- nutritional;
- elimination;
- mental health;
- informal support;
- housing and finances;
- provider agencies;
- other planning considerations.

